<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Finnish People's Delegation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Finnish People's Delegation was the revolutionary government of the Red side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-civil-war">Finnish Civil War</a>, formed by the Social Democrats when the Red Guards seized Helsinki on 28 January 1918. Chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kullervo-manner">Kullervo Manner</a>, it ruled the industrial south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> and proclaimed the Finnish Socialist Workers' Republic. After the defeats of April 1918 it withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyborg">Viipuri</a> and then fled to Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/finnish-peoples-delegation.jpg" alt="Finnish People's Delegation" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Suomen kansanvaltuuskunta · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suomen_kansanvaltuuskunta_seal_1918.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
